From: LIVI OS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Keep menu touch dragging working without panel size

Upstream-Status: Pending

Some panels, including the Waveshare 7.9" HDMI touchscreen used with LIVI,
report a 0x0 mm size in their EDID. Wayland compositors then advertise a
0 mm wl_output and RetroArch computes an infinite DPI. The menu drag
threshold becomes 65535 px, so every touch swipe is treated as a tap.

Treat a 0 mm Wayland output as unknown metrics, and give menu pointer
input a standard 96 DPI fallback so drag and swipe gestures still work.

--- a/gfx/common/wayland_common.c
+++ b/gfx/common/wayland_common.c
@@ -445,6 +445,14 @@
          break;
       };
 
+   /* wl_output reports 0 mm when the panel EDID has no size; treat
+    * that as unknown instead of deriving an infinite DPI. */
+   if (!oi || !oi->physical_width || !oi->physical_height)
+   {
+      *value = 0.0f;
+      return false;
+   }
+
    switch (type)
    {
       case DISPLAY_METRIC_MM_WIDTH:
--- a/menu/menu_driver.c
+++ b/menu/menu_driver.c
@@ -1164,6 +1164,11 @@
          dpi            = 0.0f;
 #endif
 
+      /* Touch drag/swipe detection is disabled without a DPI, so assume
+       * a standard display when the panel does not report its size. */
+      if (!(dpi > 0.0f && dpi < 10000.0f))
+         dpi            = 96.0f;
+
       dpi_cached        = true;
       last_video_width  = video_width;
       last_video_height = video_height;
